  "cellLaw": [
    "Every cell names exactly one producer node and one receiving acceptance id of that producer, or is a truthful exclusion with its reason.",
    "No two cells claim the same (operation, host, profile).",
    "A tsgo-hosted cell is answered by tsgo only; a Verter-computed answer to a TS-region operation is a duplicate.",
    "No cell is a build, bundler or runtime cell; those are exclusions.",
    "No cell cites @marko/language-tools, @marko/type-check, @marko/compiler, an installed parser or syntax highlighting as product evidence.",
    "Every cell records tsgoOperations and tsgoLimitation explicitly: an empty list and null mean the cell needs no tsgo operation and has no known tsgo limitation, never 'not recorded'. On a cell not hosted by tsgo, tsgoOperations lists the checker queries its producer consumes as type-authority input; tsgo does not answer that cell, and cellLaw[2] governs only tsgo-hosted cells.",
    "Every included cell has a ratified receiving acceptance that requires proof of its operation. A null receivingAcceptance or pendingReceiver is invalid, and a cell never borrows an acceptance id that does not prove the operation. Ratifying the receiver does not qualify the feature: full-matrix promotion (MRK10-AC1) still requires an MRK9 pass or ratified exclusion for every cell."
  ],
